  "notes": "Category codes used in variants match the built-in swiss-athletics category scheme 1:1. OQ-019 closure (2026-07-15): hurdle and implement variants are now sourced from the primary Swiss Athletics WO 2026 discipline tables — §8.1.1 (Swiss championship disciplines, senior/U23/U20/U18/U16 with hurdle count/height/first-hurdle/spacing and implement masses), §8.1.2 (further disciplines incl. 300 mH and steeple variants) and §8.1.3 (U14/U12/U10). The WO senior figures coincide with the WA CR&TR specifications the earlier secondary compilation (trackandfieldapp.com, athleticsdirect.co.uk, fetched 2026-07-06) reported, closing that verification gap. U23 variants duplicate the senior specification because the WO merges the columns ('Männer / U23 M'). Hurdle layout figures are toFirst/spacing in metres; the WO's third layout figure (run-in to the finish) is not stored. This catalog is OUTDOOR-stadium scoped: the WO indoor tables (§9.1.2/§9.1.3) define DIFFERENT 60 mH layouts (5 hurdles indoor vs 6 outdoor for the same category) and indoor-only 50 m/50 mH events; encoding indoor variants would need an indoor/outdoor dimension on DisciplineVariant — deliberately out of scope here, noted in OQ-019's closure. U12/U10 hurdle heights are meet-defined ranges (60-76.2 cm and 40-60 cm; WO §8.1.3 footnote requires the height to be published in the meet announcement), so those variants carry count/layout but no fixed height. Masters hurdle/implement variants (WA Masters specifications) are not covered by the WO tables and remain unpopulated.",
